[2026-09-17 09:27:46] REQ 260917091900-133 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:27:45.914000747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7hur2tga","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 echo \"=== design refinement: how to avoid alarm fatigue on a STANDING freeze (ext1 has been frozen for hours)? The fleet-check runs 4x/day. If ext1 is frozen for 3 days, that's 12 FAILs. Options:\n1. State file like RA_STATE: first sighting = WATCH, 2nd+ = FAIL. But a freeze that persists for days would then FAIL forever.\n2. Mirror the segcensus contract: FROZEN = FAIL always (it IS a real fault -- audio is dead). The ear check already FAILs on ext1 NO-AUDIO (standing, owned by 0073). So a second standing FAIL on the same cam doubles the alarm but they're the same alarm.\n\nActually the cleanest: the ch2 FROZEN flag IS the alarm. ext1's ear-check NO-AUDIO already holds FAIL=1 standing. Adding ch2-FROZEN FAIL = same fault, two instruments. That's fine -- the point is that a NEW freeze on a DIFFERENT cam (which the ear check might miss if segments are stale-ish) gets caught at the network layer within the hour.\n\nDecision: FROZEN row = report + FAIL=1. It's a real fault every time. The alarm-fatigue concern is handled by the fact that fleet-check FAILs on ext1 anyway. And a standing freeze SHOULD keep failing -- that's the KNOWN_FAULT contract question. ext1 freeze is owned by relay 0073 (observation-only). Should I add a KNOWN_FROZEN_CH2 allowlist for ext1? \n\nLook at the KNOWN_FAULT pattern: KNOWN_FAULT_EXT1_SEG exists for the timestamp poison. The audio freeze is a DIFFERENT fault (0073). It's known and under observation. But the freeze heals (lottery) -- when it heals, the ch2 row flips to hundreds = RECOVERY = worth seeing. If I allowlist ext1, I lose the heal signal... no, the heal shows in the row itself (ch2 count goes nonzero).\n\nSimplest honest design: report every FROZEN row + FAIL. When ext1 heals, the row flips and the FAIL disappears. The standing FAIL is owned (0073). If a NEW cam freezes, its FAIL is news. The fear organ's reasons-string grep (^[A-Z-]+ FAIL) won't match these lines unless I name them right. Let me name them 'CH2-FROZEN' so they surface in the fear reasons. ===\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:27:45.914157397Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:27:46.003319723Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8574931058,"prompt_eval_count":90193,"prompt_eval_cached_count":80640,"eval_count":542}\n(dd96d817bac7cd1b7128a2725b6819c1 . 623)
