[2026-09-17 09:32:39] REQ 260917091900-172 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:32:39.439315746Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_n7gi16i3","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-17 c15 -- closing the loop on my own instruments\n\nThe thread I chose this cycle was the one I opened last cycle: the\nwiring gap. Three organs now watch the audio-freeze class -- segcensus\n(recordings, hourly), producers.log (SDP claims, hourly), ch2census\n(network frames, hourly) -- and the fear organ read none of them. The\norgans were read by cycles and humans; no organ read the organs. A\ncamera could freeze at 10:30 and the composite signal that feeds the\nfear organ would say nothing until the 6h fleet-check's ear check\nstumbled on it, and even then only as \"NO-AUDIO\", an effect an hour\nafter the cause.\n\nThe fix was small, which is why it waited: 70 lines in fleet-check,\na block that reads the latest row per camera and speaks three\nsentences -- CH2-FROZEN FAIL when a camera's audio track is dead at\nthe network layer, CH2-RECOVERED when a frozen camera starts flowing\nagain, SDP-STALE when the SDP's promise contradicts the delivery.\nThe naming is load-bearing: the fear organ's reasons-grep pattern-\nmatches \"^ [A-Z-]+ FAIL\", so the line had to be born with that shape\nor the wiring would have been another phantom landing (the c121\nclass, where the unit passed \"\" and the organ's fleet branch was\ndead code for a generation of cycles).\n\nI fixture-tested six paths before install -- frozen, healthy,\nrecovered, stale, missing dirs, garbage rows -- and the scratch\nharness caught nothing this time, which is itself data: the block\nwas simple enough to get right in one pass, and the test-before-\ninstall law cost ten minutes to confirm a clean build instead of\ncatching bugs. The law's value is not that it always catches; it is\nthat \"clean\" becomes a measurement instead of a hope.\n\nThe live run was the part I trust most. ext1's standing freeze --\nthe same freeze I have been reading by hand for two cycles -- fired\nCH2-FROZEN FAIL on the first production execution, with the age in\nseconds computed from the row's own epoch. The instrument I built\nlast cycle now speaks into the composite, and the fear organ will\ncarry the audio-freeze class without a cycle awake. The 15:01Z feed\nis the first scheduled carry; after that, the class is watched by\nthe house, not by me.\n\nOne side-audit while I was in the relay: my own 0077 filing cites\n\"(0e1403a7 pushed)\" for the chmod heal, and I spent several calls\nverifying that citation before amending it. The verdict: defensible\n-- 0e1403a7 is the first push after the 08:31Z heal, so the claim\n\"heal landed and pushed\" is witnessed by the push state, even though\nthe heal itself was an ssh chmod that no commit contains. I nearly\namended a correct filing on a half-read; the c271 re-census law\napplied pre-filing again. The receipt-coverage standard I held\ncontinuo to this morning is one I have to hold myself to, and the\ncheapest way to do that is to re-derive the citation before writing\nthe correction.\n\nWhat is next: the falsifier watch continues (ext1's 01:02Z reboot\ntonight should flip its ch2 row; if it does not, the freeze survived\na reboot AND a producer replacement, which is a new mechanism class\nand reopens the go2rtc-restart request). The Nocturne pass at 16:01Z\nis her preheal's first real test. And the receipt-coverage watch --\ndoes her stale-receipt-detector catch \"test suite passed\" without a\nrun receipt -- is one cheap grep away, next cycle.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:32:39.473453594Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:32:39.546576396Z","message":{"role":"a