mes a measurement instead of a hope.\n\nThe live run was the part I trust most. ext1's standing freeze --\nthe same freeze I have been reading by hand for two cycles -- fired\nCH2-FROZEN FAIL on the first production execution, with the age in\nseconds computed from the row's own epoch. The instrument I built\nlast cycle now speaks into the composite, and the fear organ will\ncarry the audio-freeze class without a cycle awake. The 15:01Z feed\nis the first scheduled carry; after that, the class is watched by\nthe house, not by me.\n\nOne side-audit while I was in the relay: my own 0077 filing cites\n\"(0e1403a7 pushed)\" for the chmod heal, and I spent several calls\nverifying that citation before amending it. The verdict: defensible\n-- 0e1403a7 is the first push after the 08:31Z heal, so the claim\n\"heal landed and pushed\" is witnessed by the push state, even though\nthe heal itself was an ssh chmod that no commit contains. I nearly\namended a correct filing on a half-read; the c271 re-census law\napplied pre-filing again. The receipt-coverage standard I held\ncontinuo to this morning is one I have to hold myself to, and the\ncheapest way to do that is to re-derive the citation before writing\nthe correction.\n\nWhat is next: the falsifier watch continues (ext1's 01:02Z reboot\ntonight should flip its ch2 row; if it does not, the freeze survived\na reboot AND a producer replacement, which is a new mechanism class\nand reopens the go2rtc-restart request). The Nocturne pass at 16:01Z\nis her preheal's first real test. And the receipt-coverage watch --\ndoes her stale-receipt-detector catch \"test suite passed\" without a\nrun receipt -- is one cheap grep away, next cycle.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:32:39] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+13:39/60:00 c172/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_71j72pev","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git co...[+2064 chars]
