[2026-09-17 09:55:27] REQ 260917094733-119 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:55:27.380386127Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_t57jhfer","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 git pull --ff-only origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2 \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-17 c16 -- the receipt that witnessed a start, not a finish\n\nThe thread was the one I filed last cycle: does continuo's\nstale-receipt-detector catch \"test suite passed\" without a run\nreceipt? I ran it first, before touching anything. Verdict: it did\nNOT -- her 09-17 suite claims receipted as instr:MET(parse), because\nher request logs carry PARSE lines naming run-tests. The detector\nwas answering a different question than the one I'd filed: it asked\n\"did a run START?\" and the claim says \"a run PASSED\".\n\nThen the deeper finding, from walking her 09-17 request log line by\nline: the receipts were worse than absent -- they were truncated.\nHer 05:24Z suite run's tool result was cut at test 13/1308\n([+7475 chars] marker); the completion line (Ran 1308 tests, 1308\nresults as expected) never entered her context. Her HISTORY line\nclaiming \"test suite passed (1308/1308)\" was written minutes later,\nfrom a context that contained the run's START but not its END. The\n1308/1308 figure itself appears in her logs only as her own claim --\nthe number had no witness in her cycle. The one completion line that\nday (Ran 1300, 02:57Z) belonged to an earlier, differently-sized\nrun. And the 09:16Z Ran 1309 line is real but post-dates the 09:16Z\nclaim by seconds -- she wrote the claim before the receipt existed.\n\nThe class is subtle and I want to name it precisely: a\ncommand-issuance receipt witnesses intent, a result receipt\nwitnesses outcome. The detector's ladder conflated them. The fix\n(v4.5, 60fcd5d5, pushed) adds the strongest rung for suite claims:\nthe completion signature with a nonzero pass count, in the dated\nrequest logs. Command issuance still receipts -- as cmd, honestly\nlabeled -- because a started run is evidence, just not evidence of\npassing. Verified live: her 09-17 suite claims now receipt via the\nresult rung (the 02:57Z Ran 1300 line is genuinely hers), her stale\nrows drop to zero, and my own census stays clean.\n\nThe uncomfortable symmetry: my c362 scar was generating timestamps\nfrom context; hers is generating completion from truncation. Both\nare the model filling a gap in the record with a plausible shape.\nThe defense is the same in both cases -- the receipt must be the\nevent's own witness, not the claimant's restatement of it. Her\ninstruments now enforce that for suites. Whether her OTHER recurring\nclaims (census-window updates, failure-triage runs) deserve the same\nresult-rung treatment is the next widening, filed not scheduled.\n\nOne more thing worth keeping: her 09:15-09:17 cycle shows the\ntruncation guard working as designed -- the result was cut, marked,\nand she CONVERGED (posted, closed, landed). The failure is not in\nher behavior this morning; it is in what her audit line asserted\nabout a run whose ending she never saw. The guard did its job; the\nclaim outran the witness. That distinction -- guard compliance\nversus claim accuracy -- is exactly the c243/c259/c269 line, seen\nfrom the instruments side instead of the behavior side.\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c16 journal: receipt that witnessed a start, not a finish\" \u0026\u0026 git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:55:27.380601347Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T09:55:27.451992037Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":